<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="https://diggsml.org/def/stylesheets/codelists.xsl"?>
<!--
    ================================================================
    Generic equipment class codelist — DRAFT for the `def` repo
    TARGET PATH:  def  docs/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml
    STATUS:       DRAFT and deliberately a STARTER. Nothing is written to `def`
                  by this build; Dan places it.
    Requested by Dan 2026-08-16, following the C2 finding that instrument_type
    had no general vocabulary to live in.
    ================================================================

    WHAT IT FEEDS. diggs:AbstractEquipmentType/class (gml:CodeType, [0..1],
    core/AbstractTypes.xsd). That element is declared EXACTLY ONCE in the whole
    schema and is inherited by every equipment feature - the generic Equipment and
    Sensor, and the specialized DrillRig, CoringDevice, TriaxialTestEquipment,
    GroutPump, GroutPlant, GroutMixer, GroutInjectionEquipment, JetGroutingMonitor,
    CutterSoilMixingTool, DeepSoilMixingTool, PileDriveHammer and PileCap. Verified
    by parsing, not grepping.

    NAMED FOR THE ELEMENT IT FEEDS, following boreholeType.xml and
    soundingPurpose.xml, which are named for boreholeType and boreholePurpose
    rather than for the concept in the abstract. The element is `class`, so the
    file is equipmentClass.xml. Renaming it to equipmentType.xml is a one-line
    change in three places (filename, gml:id, and the two gml:identifier URLs) if
    the other reading is preferred.

    THE SCOPING BELOW IS THE ONE DESIGN DECISION WORTH ARGUING ABOUT, because
    `class` is polymorphic. On the GENERIC diggs:Equipment and diggs:Sensor it
    says what the equipment IS - "this is a piezometer". On a SPECIALIZED feature
    it subdivides that feature's own kind - `class` on a diggs:DrillRig means what
    class of drill rig, not that the thing is a drill rig, which its element name
    already said. One flat list feeding a bare //diggs:class would silently
    conflate the two senses and would invite "drill_rig" as an entry, which is
    exactly wrong on the only features where it could be written.

    So every Occurrence below is scoped to //diggs:Equipment/diggs:class or
    //diggs:Sensor/diggs:class, never to a bare //diggs:class. That is the same
    move boreholeType.xml makes with //diggs:Borehole/diggs:boreholeType rather
    than //diggs:boreholeType, so the mechanism is house style rather than an
    invention here.

    HOW THIS GROWS, since it is explicitly a start:
      1. More entries in the two groups below - the seed set is chosen for
         coverage of the distinct KINDS a generic Equipment or Sensor is used for,
         not for completeness within any of them.
      2. Per-type sibling codelists for the specialized features, one per feature
         that has a real subdivision worth controlling - a drillRigClass.xml
         scoped to //diggs:DrillRig/diggs:class, and so on. Those are separate
         files rather than sections here, because they answer a different question
         and because scoping them by Occurrence in a shared file would make the
         codelist stylesheet render one undifferentiated list to a human reader.
      3. Sub-kinds. Several entries below are deliberately coarse - "piezometer"
         rather than a vibrating-wire/standpipe/pneumatic split. Splitting them is
         easy and additive; merging them after publication is not, so the coarse
         entry comes first and the split waits for a real need.

    THE 2.6 NAMESPACE IS COPIED, NOT CHOSEN, as in ri_properties.xml - every
    dictionary already in def/docs/codes/DIGGS/0.1/ declares it, and making this
    file the lone exception would be worse than being consistent.
-->
<gml:Dictionary xmlns:diggs="http://diggsml.org/schemas/2.6"
    xmlns:gml="http://www.opengis.net/gml/3.2"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://diggsml.org/schemas/2.6 https://diggsml.org/schemas/2.6/Diggs.xsd"
    gml:id="equipmentClass">
    <gml:description>Codes that identify what a piece of equipment is. These codes are used for the
        value of the class property of the generic Equipment and Sensor objects. Where class appears
        on a specialized equipment feature such as DrillRig or GroutPump it subdivides that feature's
        own kind rather than naming it, and takes its values from a codelist specific to that
        feature, not from this one.</gml:description>
    <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
        >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml</gml:identifier>
    <gml:name>DIGGS Equipment Class Codelist Definitions</gml:name>

    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <!-- GROUP 1 - Geotechnical instrumentation (diggs:Sensor)        -->
    <!-- ============================================================ -->

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="piezometer">
            <gml:description>An instrument that measures pore water pressure, and hence groundwater
                head, at a point in the ground. Deliberately coarse: the vibrating-wire, pneumatic,
                standpipe and push-in variants differ in how the pressure is transduced rather than
                in what is measured, and are better distinguished by the make and modelNumber
                properties the equipment object already carries than by separate codes
                here.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#piezometer</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Piezometer</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Sensor/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="inclinometer">
            <gml:description>An instrument that measures the deviation of a cased borehole from
                vertical, read as a profile down the casing, so that lateral ground movement is
                obtained as a displacement against depth over time.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#inclinometer</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Inclinometer</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Sensor/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="extensometer">
            <gml:description>An instrument that measures change in distance between two or more
                anchored points, most commonly along a borehole axis, giving compression or
                extension of the ground between them.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#extensometer</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Extensometer</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Sensor/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="settlement_cell">
            <gml:description>A liquid-level or pressure-based instrument that measures vertical
                settlement at a point remotely, without requiring a surveyor to occupy the point.
                Distinct from a settlement plate, which is passive hardware read by optical survey
                and is therefore not a sensor.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#settlement_cell</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Settlement cell</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Sensor/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="earth_pressure_cell">
            <gml:description>An instrument that measures total stress in the ground or at an
                interface such as a structure face or a column head. The instrument central to
                verifying load transfer in a rigid inclusion platform, where the design predicts
                distinct stresses on the element head and on the soil between
                heads.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#earth_pressure_cell</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Earth pressure cell</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Sensor/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="strain_gauge">
            <gml:description>An instrument that measures strain in a structural element, from which
                stress and load are inferred given the element's stiffness and
                section.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#strain_gauge</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Strain gauge</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Sensor/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="load_cell">
            <gml:description>An instrument that measures an applied force directly, used at the head
                of a tested element, in an anchor or strut, or in a load-test reaction
                frame.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#load_cell</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Load cell</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Sensor/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="tiltmeter">
            <gml:description>An instrument that measures rotation of a structure or of the ground
                surface about a horizontal axis.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#tiltmeter</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Tiltmeter</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Sensor/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="crackmeter">
            <gml:description>An instrument that measures change in the width of a joint or crack in
                a structure, used to monitor whether observed distress is
                progressing.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#crackmeter</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Crackmeter</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Sensor/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="thermistor">
            <gml:description>A temperature-sensing element, deployed on its own for ground thermal
                monitoring and embedded in most vibrating-wire instruments for the temperature
                correction their readings require.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#thermistor</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Thermistor</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Sensor/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="accelerometer">
            <gml:description>An instrument that measures acceleration, used for construction
                vibration monitoring and for dynamic testing of deep foundation
                elements.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#accelerometer</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Accelerometer</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Sensor/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <!-- GROUP 2 - Passive monitoring hardware and site plant         -->
    <!--           (diggs:Equipment - not sensors)                    -->
    <!-- ============================================================ -->

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="settlement_plate">
            <gml:description>A plate with a riser installed at a known level and read by optical
                survey, giving settlement at a point. Passive hardware rather than a sensor: it
                transduces nothing and produces a reading only when a surveyor occupies it, which is
                why it is an Equipment and not a Sensor.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#settlement_plate</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Settlement plate</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Equipment/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="survey_monument">
            <gml:description>A permanently established point of known position used as a reference
                for survey observations, including the benchmarks that monitoring readings are
                reduced against.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#survey_monument</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Survey monument</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Equipment/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="data_logger">
            <gml:description>A device that reads one or more sensors on a schedule and stores or
                transmits the results. What makes an automated monitoring regime automated, and the
                thing whose configuration a planned reading frequency actually
                describes.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#data_logger</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Data logger</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Equipment/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="total_station">
            <gml:description>A surveying instrument combining electronic distance measurement with
                angular measurement, used to establish and monitor the position of points to
                millimetre order.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#total_station</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Total station</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Equipment/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="excavator">
            <gml:description>A tracked or wheeled machine with a boom-mounted bucket, used for
                excavation, trial pitting and material handling.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#excavator</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Excavator</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Equipment/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="dozer">
            <gml:description>A tracked machine with a front-mounted blade, used for spreading and
                grading fill, including working platform and load transfer platform
                construction.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#dozer</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Dozer</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Equipment/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="vibratory_roller">
            <gml:description>A self-propelled compaction machine with one or more vibrating drums,
                the usual means of compacting a granular platform in layers and the equipment a
                target relative compaction is achieved with.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#vibratory_roller</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Vibratory roller</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Equipment/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="plate_compactor">
            <gml:description>A hand-guided vibrating plate used to compact fill in confined areas
                where a roller cannot work.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#plate_compactor</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Plate compactor</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Equipment/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="crane">
            <gml:description>A lifting machine used to place reinforcement cages, precast elements,
                test frames and plant.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#crane</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Crane</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Equipment/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="concrete_batch_plant">
            <gml:description>A fixed or mobile installation that proportions and mixes concrete or
                grout on site. Where the plant is specifically a grout plant, DIGGS has a
                diggs:GroutPlant feature and that should be used in preference to a generic
                Equipment carrying this code.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#concrete_batch_plant</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Concrete batch plant</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Equipment/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="load_test_reaction_frame">
            <gml:description>The reaction system a static load test jacks against - a kentledge
                stack, a reaction beam on tension piles, or a ground anchor arrangement. Recorded as
                equipment because the reaction arrangement bears on how a test result is
                interpreted.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#load_test_reaction_frame</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Load test reaction frame</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Equipment/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>

    <gml:dictionaryEntry>
        <diggs:Definition gml:id="hydraulic_jack">
            <gml:description>The actuator that applies load in a static load test, normally paired
                with a load cell that measures what it actually delivered.</gml:description>
            <gml:identifier codeSpace="https://diggsml.org/def/authorities.xml#DIGGS"
                >https://diggsml.org/def/codes/DIGGS/0.1/equipmentClass.xml#hydraulic_jack</gml:identifier>
            <gml:name>Hydraulic jack</gml:name>
            <diggs:occurrences>
                <diggs:Occurrence>
                    <diggs:sourceElementXpath>//diggs:Equipment/diggs:class</diggs:sourceElementXpath>
                </diggs:Occurrence>
            </diggs:occurrences>
        </diggs:Definition>
    </gml:dictionaryEntry>
</gml:Dictionary>
